            %p
              The same is true if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing+adjoint+equivalence"} free-standing adjoint equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkFirstConditionInLackFibrationAsLiftingCondition"}
              can be compared with the definition of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
              as expressed by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting"} lifting
              condition: the condition is exactly the same, with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing+isomorphism"} free-standing isomorphism
              replaced by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing+equivalence"} free-standing equivalence
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Let us explore the second condition in Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionEquifibration"}
              a little. Note that any 1-morphism which is 2-isomorphic to an equivalence is itself an equivalence. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(h)
              is an equivalence, and condition 1. then ensures that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(h)
              lifts to an equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mo )
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\left(g'\right) = p(h)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
              must be 2-isomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              is an equivalence.
            %p
              Putting everything together, condition 2. is equivalent to: any 1-arrow of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              which maps to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              up to 2-isomorphism is an equivalence, and all equivalences of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              which map to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              up to 2-isomorphism are 2-isomorphic to one another, in such a way that, given 1-arrows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{g}: f \rightarrow p(g)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{g'}:  f \rightarrow p\left(g'\right)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo :
                    %mi g
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : g \rightarrow g'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              has the property that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\psi) = \phi_{g}^{-1} \circ \phi_{g'}
            %p
          %p
          %h2#section_References References
          %p
            The original article, speaking of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em equiv-fibrations
          %ul
            %li#Lack02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Quillen model structure for 2-categories
              %strong 26
              2 (2002) 171-205 &amp;lbrack;
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://maths.mq.edu.au/~slack/papers/qmc2cat.html"} author’s webpage
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an%3A1017.18005"} zbmath:3A1017.18005
          %p
            Beware that
            %a{:href => "#Lack02"} Lack 2002
            contains an error, not pertaining directly to the definition of a equifibration itself, but to obtaining a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Cat"} category of strict 2-categories
            with this definition (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+2-categories"} canonical model structure on 2-categories
            %a{:href => "#Lack04"} Lack 2004
            by using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing+adjoint+equivalence"} free-standing adjoint equivalence
            rather than the free-standing equivalence in the generating acyclic cofibrations:
          %ul
            %li#Lack04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Quillen model structure for bicategories
              %strong 33
              3 (2004) 185-197 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an%3A1069.18008"} Zentralblatt review
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://maths.mq.edu.au/~slack/papers/qmcbicat.html"} author’s webpage
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lack04"} Lack 2004
            = succeed ")." do
              %em fibrations
          %p
            The term
            %em equifibrations
            is used in:
          %ul
            %li#Campbell20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"}> Alexander Campbell
              \.
              = succeed "," do
                %em A homotopy coherent cellular nerve for bicategories
              %strong 368
              (2020) 107138 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.01999"}> arXiv:1907.01999
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2020.107138"} doi;10.1016/j.aim.2020.107138
          %p
            The term
            %em Lack fibrations
            is used in:
          %ul
            %li#MoserSarazolaVerdugo22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lyne+Moser"}> Lyne Moser
              , Maru Sarazola, Paulo Verdugo,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A 2Cat-inspired model structure for double categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers
              LXIII-2
              %strong 63
              2 (2022) 184-236 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.14233"}> arXiv:2004.14233
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
